  "query_preview": "..\nThrough Sunday...\n\nUpper level troughing will continue to move to the east today and\nTuesday. The surface low pressure system associated with this\ntrough will slowly move across the Canadian Prairies advecting in\nhigh pressure behind it today and Tuesday. This will bring\nslightly cooler temperatures in the 80s F and dry conditions. \n\nStarting Wednesday, upper level ridging builds in behind the\ndeparting trough shifting high pressure to the east. This pattern\nis expected to last through Friday bringing high temperatures in\nthe high 80s to low 90s F and periodic chances for showers and\nthunderstorms. Thursday is expected to bring the best chance for\nsevere thunderstorms as southeast winds advect Gulf moisture into\nMontana. It is too early to have specific details about the \ncoverage and potential hazards of these storms. \n\nEnsemble systems are indicating that the earliest the upper level\nridging pattern could be broken is next weekend. While ridging\nwill be dominant over Montana during the middle to late week\nperiod, persistent troughing will impact the Pacific Coast. \nStarting next weekend, models are indicating this trough may begin\nto move inland displacing the ridge. This is highly uncertain at \nthis time but it brings the potential for cooler temperatures by \nnext Sunday. Torgerson",
